      "problem": "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1\\end{aligned}|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1\\end{aligned}| & =-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1-4\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-4\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-5\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
